Stage 1
Beginner foundation
Alphabet and sounds, common words, pronouns, be verbs, simple sentences, basic questions, and present simple.
Goal: Understand and produce basic sentences.
Stage 2
Elementary English
Past and future forms, articles, prepositions, everyday vocabulary, and short conversations.
Goal: Handle common daily situations.
Stage 3
Intermediate English
More complex grammar, phrasal verbs, listening practice, longer writing, and expressing opinions.
Goal: Communicate independently in most familiar situations.
Stage 4
Upper-intermediate and advanced
Complex grammar, natural expressions, different accents, professional writing, debates, and nuanced vocabulary.
Goal: Communicate effectively in demanding personal, academic, and professional situations.
6. Revise and practise regularly
